ifa/issues/025 -- branch-correlation narrowing is not implemented: `a` is provably Dog in one arm and Cat in the other (the second `if flag:` correlates with the first), but only isinstance / is-None are recognised as discriminators. Emits two spurious "illegal call argument type" warnings; runtime behaviour is CORRECT on both arms, so the .check records no warnings and this flips to PASS when correlation lands.
